;; spec: docs/design/test-harness.md 1 (outline); package LIB-2 item 5a
;; expect: accept
;; result: 0
;; audit: clean
;; stage: 2
;; roots: ../../lib support
;; covers: fib.test outline
;; A 500-row outline (three columns of two types) compiles and runs. The first expansion put the steps once per row: 200 rows took 22 s to build and 400 about 85 s (the DMN agent's 400-row
;; spec: 120 s), the cost growing with the square of the rows; the macro now writes the steps once, as a function of the row, and each row is one call: 500 rows build in about 2 s. This case
;; is the regression guard: a quadratic expansion would make the case run for minutes (the cases of the gate have a timeout), and the checks that follow pin that every row is its own scenario,
;; with its own text and id, and that a failing row says which row failed.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll fib.test.core fib.test.run))

(defspecs specs
